WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.090
[...]

00:00:04.097 --> 00:00:07.357
Imagine this thought experiment.

00:00:07.366 --> 00:00:11.413
Everyone gathers in a great assembly
to vote on the principles that

00:00:11.413 --> 00:00:14.060
will govern society.

00:00:14.060 --> 00:00:17.491
But during the assembly,
everyone temporarily

00:00:17.491 --> 00:00:21.568
forgets his or her social
and economic status.

00:00:21.568 --> 00:00:26.828
You don't know your race, gender,
religion, ethnicity, or class.

00:00:26.836 --> 00:00:31.008
You don't know whether you were rich
or poor, strong or weak, healthy

00:00:31.008 --> 00:00:33.888
or unhealthy.

00:00:33.895 --> 00:00:37.325
Under these conditions,
which of these principles

00:00:37.325 --> 00:00:43.461
would you choose to govern
social and economic inequalities?

00:00:43.461 --> 00:00:47.198
One-- permit only
those inequalities that

00:00:47.198 --> 00:00:53.288
increase the overall welfare
of society, or total utility.

00:00:53.288 --> 00:00:56.773
Two-- permit only
those inequalities that

00:00:56.773 --> 00:01:00.829
benefit the least advantaged
members of society.

00:01:00.829 --> 00:01:05.633
Or three-- permit whatever
inequalities result

00:01:05.633 --> 00:01:09.863
when some people work hard and exercise
their talents more successfully

00:01:09.864 --> 00:01:14.034
than others.

